# Keep secrets and local state OUT of the image layers.
#
# The Dockerfile does `COPY . .`, and Docker reads .dockerignore from the build
# context root - without this file, a service-account key or .env sitting in the
# working tree gets baked into an image layer and leaks to anyone who can pull
# or inspect the image. Nothing here is needed at build time: docker-compose
# injects the environment via env_file: and mounts the GCP key read-only.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
app/gcp-credentials.json
*-credentials.json
gcp-credentials*.json

.git
.gitignore
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
data/
*.db
*.sqlite3
*.log
.venv/
venv/
